[
    {
        "content": "<p>This is probably a question for <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"221653\">@Paul Reichert</span> or <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260921\">@Julia Markus Himmel</span>, but everybody is welcome to help. I’m reviving an ancient Lean program that contained the following code:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">collapseSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" \"</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intercalate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">split</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Char</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isWhitespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"n\">isEmpty</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">collapseSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Foo   bar   baz\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- \"Foo bar baz\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which no longer works. I know I can refuse progress and write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">collapseSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" \"</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intercalate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Iter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toString</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">split</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Char</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isWhitespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"n\">isEmpty</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>saying I don’t want to hear about <code>String.Slice</code> or iterators. I guess this is probably not the intended fix. My question is: what is the current idiomatic way of doing this? Is there any kind of migration guide somewhere? I understand we probably don’t want to clutter the Lean manual with such guides, but maybe there are some blog posts somewhere?</p>",
        "id": 625233694,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1789735959
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well you can keep almost everything with a slight reorder:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">collapseSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">split</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Char</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isWhitespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">!·.</span><span class=\"n\">isEmpty</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">intercalateString</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" \"</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">collapseSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Foo   bar   baz\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- \"Foo bar baz\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 625234461,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1789736159
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, Robin's approach is the intended one. I have an outline for a post explaining everything around the new String API, but unfortunately I haven't found the time to write it yet.</p>",
        "id": 625234904,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1789736267
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Very nice, I was indeed missing <code>Std.Iter.intercalateString</code>.</p>",
        "id": 625236724,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1789736682
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 625236751,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1789736688
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another case that comes up is things like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"a b c\"</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">split</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Yes\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"No\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here, I guess I cannot really avoid going to lists, right?</p>",
        "id": 625238417,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1789737068
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Or should I try to consume pieces from the iterator until I have enough?</p>",
        "id": 625238609,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1789737106
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, unfortunately we don't have nice syntax (yet) for matching on the first few results returned by an iterator. A slightly better option is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"a b c\"</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">split</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">take</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Yes\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"No\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>By <code>take</code>ing the number of elements you're actually going to examine you make sure that you only scan the string as far as necessary, unlike the old <code>List</code>-based <code>split</code> and your snippet which both always process the entire string even though the two spaces might be right at the start.</p>",
        "id": 625240663,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1789737576
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another small detail: the <code>split</code> function can take either a predicate, or a <code>Char</code>, or a <code>String</code> as the separator, so you don't need to write <code>\"a b c\".split (' ' == ·)</code>. <code>\"a.b.c\".split ' '</code> is sufficient.</p>",
        "id": 625241017,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1789737664
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 625244204,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1789738420
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"260921\">Julia Markus Himmel</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Iterators.20and.20slices/near/625240663\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes, unfortunately we don't have nice syntax (yet) for matching on the first few results returned by an iterator. A slightly better option is</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"a b c\"</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">split</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">take</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Yes\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"No\"</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><del>(I believe this should be <code>take 3</code>, otherwise the first case won't trigger. Agreed otherwise.)</del></p>\n<p>My bad, the example is exactly right and I was just confused.</p>",
        "id": 625245057,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Reichert",
        "timestamp": 1789738645
    }
]